From 15ef9412b516a3dd814b812e64e307966a064f25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:48:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cron): a slow state.db write no longer crashes cron
 finalization [daveey]

The fallback-title lookup (get_next_title_in_lineage) ran through the bounded
SessionDB proxy without its own try. After the first title write timed out
(another process held the WAL write lock), the proxy failed fast and that
RuntimeError escaped _finalize_cron_session: run_job crashed after the turn
finished, the row stayed untitled and unended, and agent teardown was skipped
(hermes-hub x-reply-discovery, 2026-10-28).

- _finalize_cron_session never raises; title fallbacks are built guarded.
- run_job's finally guards the call so teardown / hand-off always runs.
- On a proxy timeout, log one WARNING naming job + session and retry title +
  end_session once on a fresh SessionDB connection in a daemon thread
  (cron.finalize_retry_delay_seconds, default 30s; same cleanup bound).
- tests/cron/test_cron_finalize_slow_write.py (4 tests, red before).
